{"title":"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems\">2008 AMC 12A #22</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2008 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">2008 AMC 10A #25</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(without_trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (without trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(simply_Pythagorean_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (simply Pythagorean Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(coordinate_bashing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (coordinate bashing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Answer_Choices_&amp;_Estimation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Answer Choices &amp; Estimation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A round table has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Six rectangular place mats are placed on the table. Each place mat has width <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> as shown. They are positioned so that each mat has two corners on the edge of the table, these two corners being end points of the same side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Further, the mats are positioned so that the inner corners each touch an inner corner of an adjacent mat. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/455ee9e9f5150b8651dd85c1adc2f62d3193a852.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]unitsize(4mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8)+fontsize(8)); draw(Circle((0,0),4)); path mat=(-2.687,-1.5513)--(-2.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,-1.5513)--cycle; draw(mat); draw(rotate(60)*mat); draw(rotate(120)*mat); draw(rotate(180)*mat); draw(rotate(240)*mat); draw(rotate(300)*mat); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(-1.55,2.1),E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(-0.5,3.8),S);[/asy]\" width=\"155\" height=\"155\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a857eb25cecf123d4bb291b0b16f7cba312990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 2\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 3\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 2\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\frac{5+2\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"570\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Trigonometry)\">Solution 1 (Trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let one of the mats be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, and the center be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as shown: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/621f102520744d9e379a054f5031a004f090acff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]unitsize(8mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8)+fontsize(8)); draw(Circle((0,0),4)); path mat=(-2.687,-1.5513)--(-2.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,-1.5513)--cycle; draw(mat); draw(rotate(60)*mat); draw(rotate(120)*mat); draw(rotate(180)*mat); draw(rotate(240)*mat); draw(rotate(300)*mat); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(-1.55,2.1),E); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(0.03,1.5),E); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,(-3.6,2.5513),E); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,(-3.15,1.35),E); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,(0.05,3.20),E); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,(-0.75,4.15),E); label(&quot;\\(O\\)&quot;,(0.00,-0.10),E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(-0.1,3.8),S); label(&quot;\\(4\\)&quot;,(-0.4,2.2),S); draw((0,0)--(0,3.103)); draw((0,0)--(-2.687,1.5513)); draw((0,0)--(-0.5,3.9686));[/asy]\" width=\"305\" height=\"318\" />\n</p><p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mats, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/dde7e41e64e179118496632f6d02168c25005f18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta BOC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral\" title=\"Equilateral\">equilateral</a> (the hexagon with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is regular). So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/1161ca46884a612ac5510ecc8378a6e9478ac31c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=CO=x$\" width=\"116\" height=\"12\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32bee7cd793b89d6a60f411fb8cebfda37d9b48f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OCD = \\angle OCB + \\angle BCD = 60^\\circ+90^\\circ=150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"372\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c86b0ba1dbc6e9482c2800a4b78849d2e532f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2=1^2+x^2-2\\cdot1\\cdot x \\cdot \\cos(150^\\circ) \\Rightarrow x^2 + x\\sqrt{3} - 15 = 0 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{-\\sqrt{3}\\pm 3\\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"597\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c07c16f2dd0533d3c6e64983ec6b81de3e41caad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{3\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\Rightarrow (C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"173\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28without_trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(without_trigonometry)\">Solution 2 (without trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (without trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/46569d6dd3fa86f698827e8de15b0480e1733d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> as in the diagram. Draw the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and call the intersection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46d563ae07e49e4af0f1efbe581e11a5eab9f6d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]unitsize(8mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8)+fontsize(8)); draw(Circle((0,0),4)); path mat=((-2.687,-1.5513)--(-2.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,-1.5513)--cycle); draw(mat); draw(rotate(60)*mat); draw(rotate(120)*mat); draw(rotate(180)*mat); draw(rotate(240)*mat); draw(rotate(300)*mat); pair D = rotate(300)*(-3.687,1.5513); pair C = rotate(300)*(-2.687,1.5513); pair EE = foot((0.00,0.00),D,C); draw(D--EE--(0,0)); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(-1.55,2.1),E); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(0.03,1.5),E); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,(-3.6,2.5513),E); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,(-3.15,1.35),E); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,(0.05,3.20),E); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,(-0.75,4.15),E); label(&quot;\\(O\\)&quot;,(0.00,-0.10),E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(-0.1,3.8),S); label(&quot;\\(4\\)&quot;,(-0.4,2.2),S); draw((0,0)--(0,3.103)); draw((0,0)--(-2.687,1.5513)); draw((0,0)--(-0.5,3.9686)); label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;, EE,SE); [/asy]\" width=\"305\" height=\"318\" />\n</p><p>As proved in the first solution, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feb8d3a205963ac15d9abef4e32542b8fb0ed44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OCD = 150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />. \nThat makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64ae1aba1d51614a94bb746d8a87f522fd0a29e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta OCE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb2805e876c38af281f45133da2ca0ca199c1311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OE = \\frac{x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca5927ade66d4aed0fdbb7ae115d898773e755c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE= \\frac{x\\sqrt 3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54d991d9a77641375f44bdfef0ce7c584d895c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ODE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is a right triangle, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/9706e3d2915ebd20e7f3ff106587854b35655fe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left({\\frac{x}{2}}\\right)^2 + \\left({\\frac{x\\sqrt 3}{2} +1}\\right)^2 = 4^2 \\Rightarrow  x^2+x\\sqrt3-15 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"387\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/b/fabfee4bf61a40361f0ee1b0086a02f7bdbb41b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x =\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\Rightarrow (C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"173\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28simply_Pythagorean_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(simply_Pythagorean_Theorem)\">Solution 3 (simply Pythagorean Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (simply Pythagorean Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf947194401dc9c72a5daeb8da4b913ce09437c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]unitsize(8mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8)+fontsize(8)); draw(Circle((0,0),4)); path mat=(-2.687,-1.5513)--(-2.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,-1.5513)--cycle; draw(mat); draw(rotate(60)*mat); draw(rotate(120)*mat); draw(rotate(180)*mat); draw(rotate(240)*mat); draw(rotate(300)*mat); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(-1.55,2.1),E); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(0.03,1.5),E); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,(-3.6,2.5513),E); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,(-3.15,1.35),E); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,(0.05,3.20),E); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,(-0.75,4.15),E); label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;,(0,4.17)); label(&quot;\\(F\\)&quot;,(0.75,4.15),W); label(&quot;\\(O\\)&quot;,(0.00,-0.10),E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(-0.1,3.8),S); label(&quot;\\(4\\)&quot;,(-0.4,2.2),S); draw((0,0)--(0,3.103)); draw((0,0)--(-2.687,1.5513)); draw((0,0)--(-0.5,3.9686)); draw((0,0)--(-0.5,3.9686));[/asy]\" width=\"305\" height=\"318\" />\n</p><p>By symmetry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db9d3474e139c8e1c2f5902c3cb42d7e47fa7e0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is an extension of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e9722aa8c442b2bbeb879308bfb8ebb9bf7395a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OED = 90^\\circ$\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e904087457a88014363180df5884120c138ff7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06b72e8768a697f0ebb50f8958d347cd4b64168.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a58af7cba0d57282af2cb59954b6e1fad9e718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OE = \\sqrt{16-\\frac{1}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{63}}{2} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{7}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"246\" height=\"43\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d6098ce09f6f2b36bb447d30083315c8c0ca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CED$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc46dfe37f06829c14c0a2a5a061221b5656c216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" /> (this can also be deduced from Pythagoras on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d6098ce09f6f2b36bb447d30083315c8c0ca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CED$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />).\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea3e11cdf92b798b4c4f99174eac6a23e12777e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC = \\frac{3\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"135\" height=\"41\" />. As previous solutions noted, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/41752e67cd033c961edd7532c9376bc82296d255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BOC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral, and thus the desired length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c58338f2d21547094cb82a9c1c10c88fa68b4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = OC \\implies (C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/841fc12191c627307cb69381b7e062642d59896d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]unitsize(8mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8)+fontsize(8)); draw(Circle((0,0),4)); path mat=(-2.687,-1.5513)--(-2.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,-1.5513)--cycle; draw(mat); draw(rotate(60)*mat); draw(rotate(120)*mat); draw(rotate(180)*mat); draw(rotate(240)*mat); draw(rotate(300)*mat); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(-1.95,3),E); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,(-3.6,2.5513),E); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,(0.05,3.20),E); label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;,(0.40,-3.60),E); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,(-0.75,4.15),E); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,(-2.62,1.5),E); label(&quot;\\(F\\)&quot;,(-2.64,-1.43),E); label(&quot;\\(G\\)&quot;,(-0.2,-2.8),E); label(&quot;\\( \\sqrt{3}x\\)&quot;,(-1.5,-0.5),E); label(&quot;\\(M\\)&quot;,(-2,-0.9),E); label(&quot;\\(O\\)&quot;,(0.00,-0.10),E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(-2.7,2.3),S); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(0.1,-3.4),S); label(&quot;\\(8\\)&quot;,(-0.3,0),S); draw((0,-3.103)--(-2.687,1.5513)); draw((0.5,-3.9686)--(-0.5,3.9686));[/asy]\" width=\"305\" height=\"318\" />\n</p><p>Looking at the diagram above, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is a diameter of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> due to symmetry. Due to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Thales%27_theorem\" title=\"Thales&#39; theorem\">Thales' theorem</a>, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is a right triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/318e45bc83596fa6ee365ddba778abf861a99a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 90 ^\\circ$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e195ed4818e368e25b7cb6e335e24d0613ba50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e538978649c14e1616fac744e983b5981d0ea8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is also a right angle. To find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf9409044fef7f3966027eec40b2cced52eb16c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />, notice that if we draw a line from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, the midpoint of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf9409044fef7f3966027eec40b2cced52eb16c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />, it creates two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangles. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84657409a0d1fb9f6e0e80ce9f4bb6ed5183b73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD = MG = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}x}{2} \\Rightarrow DG = \\sqrt{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"273\" height=\"41\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb49432a4a8ae07321aad985c9023065280738c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = 2 + \\sqrt{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Applying the Pythagorean theorem to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0b50479c5ea5d1547dba41aa7903660b135bf23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2+\\sqrt{3}x)^2 + x^2 = 8^2 \\Rightarrow 4 + 3x^2 + 4\\sqrt{3}x + x^2 = 64 \\Rightarrow x^2 + \\sqrt{3}x - 15 = 0\\]\" width=\"521\" height=\"21\" /> Using the quadratic formula to solve, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/7/ec789bc2d89d3aef65c6e4f53856ba4222c1c76e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{-\\sqrt{3} \\pm \\sqrt{3 -4(1)(-15)}}{2} = \\frac{\\pm 3\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\]\" width=\"347\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be positive, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75cff19c3a77f6b1e1516177a0eebc57ffffdfa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{3\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{3}}{2} \\Rightarrow (C)\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~Zeric Hang\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28coordinate_bashing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(coordinate_bashing)\">Solution 5 (coordinate bashing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (coordinate bashing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4cdbc1bb063bb8e933278422d4f2bf6f97c1505.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]unitsize(8mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8)+fontsize(8)); draw(Circle((0,0),4)); path mat=(-2.687,-1.5513)--(-2.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,-1.5513)--cycle; draw(mat); draw(rotate(60)*mat); draw(rotate(120)*mat); draw(rotate(180)*mat); draw(rotate(240)*mat); draw(rotate(300)*mat); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(-1.55,2.1),E); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(-0.5,3.8),S);[/asy]\" width=\"305\" height=\"305\" />\n</p><p>We will let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e3b2bed68368fd0beec505935098ace79ee8022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> be the origin. This way the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a40d2badbac4bdd4c5ffb5628c2e13a071bd14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" />. By <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" />, the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a86e5db998a2bde546660965f87dc82a803d2d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}, y + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"125\" height=\"55\" />. The distance any point with coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> is from the origin is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c0688227c7a4c52edfc3dfbb79cf828c9e555c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"22\" />. Therefore, the distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is from the origin is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/874b170a17885e8d5a170726e385d2eed6dedffb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + x^2 + x\\sqrt{3} + \\frac{3}{4} = x^2 + x\\sqrt{3} + 1 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"317\" height=\"38\" />. We get the quadratic equation mentioned in solution 2. Using the quadratic formula, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c07c16f2dd0533d3c6e64983ec6b81de3e41caad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{3\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\Rightarrow (C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"173\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Note: Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are not labeled in the diagram, refer to solution 1 for the location of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/9/ff92da940d0dc47ed066383177bf3f4a5eca0753.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]unitsize(8mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8)+fontsize(8)); draw(Circle((0,0),4)); path mat=(-2.687,-1.5513)--(-2.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,1.5513)--(-3.687,-1.5513)--cycle; draw(mat); draw(rotate(60)*mat); draw(rotate(120)*mat); draw(rotate(180)*mat); draw(rotate(240)*mat); draw(rotate(300)*mat); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,(-1.55,2.1),E); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,(-3.6,2.5513),E); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,(-3.15,1.35),E); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,(0.05,3.20),E); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,(-0.75,4.15),E); label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;,(0.3,4.15),E); label(&quot;\\(F\\)&quot;,(-3.4,1.89),E); draw((0.5,3.9686)--(-3.13,2.45)); draw((0.5,3.9686)--(-2.95,2));[/asy]\" width=\"305\" height=\"318\" />\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb4ef5e92125766dc6d4e5e343d11a495575a6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overarc{AE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"23\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8b7dd31c63b399cd72fe186a628adba5df3cad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> the circumference of the circle. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8bc36793a7c64d05fff20d519f0f72d9256fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> is the side length of an inscribed hexagon with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f2628c7bd8aba6794daadad02ce8f46d94c15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is a right triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/3862ef4fbb3e33acaa1d35f5e1a73a4ebff928ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AF}=\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1511aa3f29f92291f7fd06338b5f0390f8182bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EF}=x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"43\" />. Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, we get\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39f737bafb6451209f160699a5a9e713cded2a4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2 = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"204\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p><br />\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd2d2418da65e0a4e41e6cfb91dd4c466a7cf06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{3\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\ \\boxed{\\text{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Answer_Choices_.26_Estimation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Answer_Choices_&amp;_Estimation)\">Solution 7 (Answer Choices &amp; Estimation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Answer Choices &amp; Estimation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The smallest distance between the intersection between two adjacent placemats and the circle is a bit less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the answer will be a bit more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e27edeb7146c09c76ae6147e1a8e8278a25ab92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-1=3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> Going up, we guess that the next one up is the answer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed5ef208871ddbcd8388009251cc73ca8c7e5fde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"43\" /> which is about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb85407fb427776f0b8c43c80bf707d7b99f8c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />. The next one up after that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/8507577cef9e6c795c9fc858a8758367e71c8a90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"23\" /> which is about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b8245e043508c7c928c89b42f9ce38f04d720d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> and seems too big. So we circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/0/b60a9b31d97b25bd240223cbafcbc476373bc836.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C) }\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"127\" height=\"54\" /> and are happy we just cheesed the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/01927bf7bbcf5688067a91087d440c77879049b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/c/abc1744a459ad135efd3fd45fca7285cae133717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> problem <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc7bd42e6cb90851b324c8f2955a8d3021b6cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" c